  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "The bones' orbits and tumbling, the spirits, the funnel's streaks and sway, and the frost and sigil textures change per cast. The storm's timing stays fixed."
  },
  "director_notes": "From Lisa's spells01 image, Necromancer - Bone Tempest: 'the dead rise, death takes all'. Built on the tornado's vortex, but squat and wide (a tempest over an area, not a travelling twister) and additive, so it reads as ghost-light, not dust. Bones use the new sparks look: bone, attached to the vortex so they climb and orbit and are flung out at the scatter beat. Spirit wisps are long-streaked embers orbiting faster. Element shadow (death magic) in the spells01 icy cyan palette."
